<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72029" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅδ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>belonging to a way</i> or <i>journey,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνις ὅ.</span> a bird <i>of omen for
				the journey</i> (or <i>seen by the way</i>), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				157
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ. κράτος
			αἴσιον</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				104
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑρμῆς ὅ.</span> H.
				<i>the guardian of roads and travellers,</i> whose statues
			stood on the road-side, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅδιον, τό,</span>
			<i>travelling expenses,</i> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Inscr.Magn.</u>
				52.39
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
